{"abstract":"This paper reports from an ongoing research project on meaningful adoption and use of Generative Artificial Intelligence within the Communication Department of a Danish Municipality. Given its capacity to generate images, information, and text, GenAI models are positioned as being potentially transformative to cognitive tasks in knowledge work, raising concerns about skill displacement and a loss of meaning in the profession. This paper presents a set of sociotechnical principles for the introduction and integration of novel technologies, such as GenAI, while retaining meaningfulness in work. These principles were crafted by combining work design theory and extensive empirical material gathered through Action Design Research, in close collaboration with employees from the department. Centering the need for a common understanding of expectations for GenAI, the principles also point to the importance of organizational support to enable autonomous experimentation and accountability, while emphasizing transparency surrounding the decision-making process for the use of GenAI.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","Marttila, Sanna-Maria","Sandbukt, Sunniva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759406"],"event":{"acronym":"ECIS","title":"European Conference on Information Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Action Design Research","Generative AI","Sociotechnical Principles","Work design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crafting meaningful generative ai enabled knowledge work","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106309094/Crafting_Meaningful_Generative_AI-Enabled_Knowledge_Work.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759406","ids":["itu-6aac332a-122b-4b49-a315-91b5cb88a459"],"keyword":["Action Design Research","Generative AI","Sociotechnical Principles","Work design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-567D1CDC6155A62357BE8A87B85C5BF4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106309094/Crafting_Meaningful_Generative_AI-Enabled_Knowledge_Work.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanna-Maria","key":"marttilapau","last":"Marttila","locid":"528393a3-e784-47a8-85be-c81d44c393bd","name":"Marttila, Sanna-Maria","orcid":"0000-0003-3793-5021","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sunniva","key":"sandbuktpau","last":"Sandbukt","locid":"06d038a4-f659-4c53-8a6d-58e295ab603f","name":"Sandbukt, Sunniva","orcid":"0009-0002-4274-4991","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00000034"],"issue":"2024","journal":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","paperid":"10","status":"p","title":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems","title_org":"Proceedings / European Conference on Information Systems (ECIS)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6aac332a-122b-4b49-a315-91b5cb88a459"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Crafting Meaningful Generative AI-Enabled Knowledge Work","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759406","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Within the domain of Information Systems, assumptions around sociotechnical change cohesively build on establishing a stable and balanced relationship between the social and technical structures. When these structures become too rigid, revolutionary moments that punctuate the status quo are required for the structures to accommodate to a new situation. Approaching sociotechnical change with “punctuation of equilibrium” is becoming increasingly ineffective. In line with rising instability and rapid digital development, we argue that new sociotechnical change approaches are needed. In this paper we investigate how individual knowledge workers respond to the increasingly complex challenges they face when orchestrating social and technical structures to support efficient and creative knowledge work. We suggest a new perspective that covers an unstable equilibrium emerging from the interplay between individuals and their usage of “the collection of rigid and flexible workplace technologies”. Our study is based on data from interviews made with 40 knowledge professionals over a period of three years, inquiring into individual experiences with sociotechnical change. Our study reveals contradictory patterns of both technological-individualisation and -socialisation. A universal generative mechanism emerges when these patterns complement each other and generates continuous change that seems to diminish inertia from rigid structures while also intensifying agile responses.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Baskerville, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695300"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Georgia State University"],"keyword":["Critical realism","Generative mechanisms","Sociotechnical change","deep and surface structures","unstable equilibrium"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"explaining sociotechnical change an unstable equilibrium perspective","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85124105547","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695300","identifier":[{"id":"85124105547","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-dc7e6bde-cbcc-4dbe-8429-97e36b37a87c"],"keyword":["Sociotechnical change","critical realism","deep and surface structures","generative mechanisms","unstable equilibrium"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B0594BCB0DA7B313539E2E94681D76F8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"georgia state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0960085x.2021.2023669","issn":["0960085X","14769344"],"issn_org":["0960085X"],"issue":"4","journal":"European Journal of Information Systems","pages":"634-652","publisher":"Palgrave Macmillan","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Information Systems","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124105547"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-dc7e6bde-cbcc-4dbe-8429-97e36b37a87c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Explaining Sociotechnical Change: An Unstable Equilibrium Perspective","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695300","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Velkommen til antologien “Studier af relevante og tidstypiske digitale udfordringer i en dansk/nordisk kontekst.” Antologien er rettet til ledere og ansvarlige for digitaliseringsaktiviteter i danske virksomheder og organisationer, som er nysgerrige på den forskning, der foregår på IT-universitetets institut ”Business IT”. Vi har samlet en række artikler som viser et bredt udsnit af den forskning som foregår på instituttet Business IT - i daglig tale kaldet BIT. BIT har et større antal forskere, der til dagligt forsker og underviser i de mange aspekter og bevægelser, som digitalisering afføder i samfundet og i offentlige som private virksomheder. Oftest er vores artikler på engelsk. Mange af forskerne er internationale og kommer fra forskellige regioner i verdenen. Sammen deltager vi på konferencer i udlandet og udgiver i engelsksprogede tidsskrifter. Med denne udgivelse har vi valgt at gøre noget ved den engelsksprogede formidlingstradition, idet vi som et eksperiment har fået oversat otte artikler til dansk af bureauet Hurtigoversætter. Vi mener de otte artikler er relevante og aktuelle i en dansk kontekst, og så dækker de bredt over hvad BIT-forskerne interesserer sig for og forsker i. Studierne spænder bredt i både deres tilgang inden for forskningsområderne: Informationssystemer (IS), Computer Supported Cooperative Work (CSCW) og Science and Technology Studies (STS). Ligeledes er der anvendt forskellige dataindsamlingsmetoder såsom etnografiske studier, casestudier og kvantitative undersøgelser. I samlingen finder du således studier om anvendelse af digitalisering på samfundsplan samt på organisationsplan i såvel private som offentlige virksomheder. Nogle studier har fokus på implementering af bestemte platformsteknologier eller teknologier som blockchain, AI eller fænomener som e-valg. Andre handler om ledelsesopgaven i relation til digitaliseringsstrategier og innovation, ledelse af medarbejdere under Covid-19 eller udfordringer med teknostress i forbindelse med den stigende digitalisering.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383872"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blockchain","Computer Supported Cooperative Work CSCW","Digitalization","Information systems IS","Science and Technology Studies STS"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"studier af relevante og tidstypiske digital udfordringer i en dansk nordisk kontekst en forskningsantologi fra business it instituttet på it universitetet i københavn","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92516192/BIT_bog_2023_Studier_af_digitale_udfordringer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383872","ids":["itu-b2bc6242-2556-4729-8434-850b991b86a9"],"keyword":["Blockchain","Computer Supported Cooperative Work (CSCW)","Digitalization","Information Systems (IS)","Science and Technology Studies (STS)"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4E800E0E58E547BC3A4DC6809B201F36"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92516192/BIT_bog_2023_Studier_af_digitale_udfordringer.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerped","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenped","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"54728da8-274d-40e6-b119-23318d995721","name":"Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh","orcid":"0000-0002-0158-5034","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788779496484"],"pages":"139","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b2bc6242-2556-4729-8434-850b991b86a9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Studier af relevante og tidstypiske digital udfordringer i en dansk/nordisk kontekst : en forskningsantologi fra Business IT-instituttet på IT-Universitetet i København","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383872","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"A well-designed information system (IS) in the classical view comprises two interrelated yet different subsystems; one that represents the technological dimension of work; and one that represents the social dimension. When these subsystems are heralded as equally important, they constitute a sociotechnical whole, producing economic outcomes such as profit and efficiency, plus humanistic outcomes, such as engagement and well-being. We see, increasingly, this classical view becoming obliviated. In this conceptual paper, we reflect upon the role of humans and technology in these changing work environments. While technical aspects from Artificial Intelligence and digital technologies are dominating the social side of work, we suggest a sociotechnical reversal to happen. Whereas this technosocial reality might be well motivated by advances in efficiency and productivity, the effects on well-being and engagement are less well understood. Consequently, we provide a set of theoretically derived principles to guide these changes in the digital workplace.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Wunderlich, Nico","Baskerville, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384280"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["AI","Digital work","Human values","socio technical principles","techno social reality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"artificial intelligence and digital work","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92452241/Artificial_Intelligence_and_Digital_Work_The_Sociotechnical_Reversal.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384280","ids":["itu-cdc1bf59-0a0c-4761-b0ad-ec484c91f51a"],"keyword":["AI","digital work","human values","socio-technical principles","techno-social reality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3DA30449A72E777DD81B9F5655C8D6CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/4fa6eece-c043-4ea4-bd59-8f49bd445878/content","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92452241/Artificial_Intelligence_and_Digital_Work_The_Sociotechnical_Reversal.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nico","key":"wunderlichpau","last":"Wunderlich","name":"Wunderlich, Nico","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard","key":"baskervillepau","last":"Baskerville","name":"Baskerville, Richard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cdc1bf59-0a0c-4761-b0ad-ec484c91f51a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Artificial Intelligence and Digital Work","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384280","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
