{"abstract":"Structuring workplaces within a socio-technical paradigm aims for both efficiency and worker wellbeing. However, with the swift integration of digital and emerging technologies, maintaining this balance has become demanding. Current trends suggest a lag in the social system's adaptation to rapid IT investments, resulting in reduced job engagement and notable Digital Transformation (DT) setbacks. To address the unrealized potential, this study advocates integrating the socio-technical approach with the socio-economic theory of hidden costs. We quantify these concealed expenditures from DT initiatives in nine Scandinavian companies. We introduce the concept of a 'shadow' to illustrate how economic focus in DT-projects can obscure aspects of social costs. Our objective is to delineate a research agenda that underscores a balance between economic and humanistic aims within the sociotechnical context.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Monod, Emmanuel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718853"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Shanghai University of International Business and Economics"],"keyword":["Digital transformation","Hidden costs","SHADOW","Sociotechnical"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the long shadows from digital transformation initiatives a research agenda","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102874892/paper16.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718853","identifier":[{"id":"85181085963","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4c9523bf-327b-44cf-b5b6-e5359a01dded"],"keyword":["Sociotechnical,","digital transformation","hidden costs","shadow"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-BD6726BDAB94BD4EA28DF71E39E198FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102874892/paper16.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"shanghai university of international business and economics","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Shanghai University of International Business and Economics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emmanuel","key":"monodpau","last":"Monod","name":"Monod, Emmanuel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","pages":"184-191","publisher":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181085963"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4c9523bf-327b-44cf-b5b6-e5359a01dded"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Long Shadows from Digital Transformation Initiatives: A Research Agenda","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718853","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"I meget digitaliserede lande som Danmark, viser statistikken, at en ud af fire ansatte har oplevet højestressniveauer. Dog er viden om dette fænomen, på trods af omfattende forskningsbeviser for tilstedeværelsen af technostress, endnu ikke en del af materialet og vejledningerne fra officielle myndigheder. Tidligere forskning i technostress har givet kvantitative psykologiske og neurofysiologiske perspektiver på technostress med fokus på individet, teknologien eller det teknologiske miljø. Vi betragter dette som en begrænset tilgang, da den udelukker det sociale miljø, hvor technostress opstår. Vores hensigt er at vise de sociologiske mekanismer, som bidrager til technostress ved at bruge en sociologisk pligtlinse. Vi spørger: 'Hvilken viden kan den sociologiske pligtlinse tilføre den teoretiske forståelse af technostress?' Til at besvare vores forskningsspørgsmål bruger vi et indlejret casestudie i Danmark ved at se på det eksisterende politiske materiale og interviews med 14 ansatte fra seks forskellige organisationer. Vi mener, at stress i praksis mest betragtes fra et responsperspektiv, som peger på individet. Denne synsvinkel er en iboende del af, hvordan individer tager ansvar for den technostress, de oplever. Et andet kritisk resultat fra vores data er, at technostress er socialt konstrueret. Vores teoretiske bidrag er anvendelsen af en for IS ukendt teori, og en kvalitativ tilgang til forskning i technostress, som giver os mulighed for at afdække, hvordan den sociale pligtkonstruktion påvirker den enkelte ansatte. Vores teoretiske bidrag peger på behovet for en praksis, som bevæger sig i retning af at betragte technostress som et samfundsmæssigt snarere end et udelukkende individuelt ansvar.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Stana, Raluca","Nicolajsen, Hanne Westh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381703"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["teknostress"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sociologiske mekanismer bag ikt relateret technostress på arbejdspladsen","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/92516192/BIT_bog_2023_Studier_af_digitale_udfordringer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381703","ids":["itu-1d258262-d15e-49b8-9ca9-921bbd99916f"],"keyword":["teknostress"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6042A829832BFC5D8B5288AF072B201F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/92516192/BIT_bog_2023_Studier_af_digitale_udfordringer.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raluca","key":"stanapau","last":"Stana","name":"Stana, Raluca","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne Westh","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"