{"abstract":"The workplace is changing rapidly and knowledge work is conducted increasingly in settings that are global, digital, flat and networked. The epicenter of value-creation are the individuals and their interactions. Unified Communication and Collaboration Technology (UC&C) supports individual interactions, collaboration and knowledge creation. The use of this technology is growing globally. In a previous study, we found that UC&C in collocated and distributed settings, produced misfits and fits between situated enacted practice-use of UC&C and the experienced productivity. We respond to the KITA 2015 call with this work-in-progress paper. We apply the IT Knowledge Artefact (ITKA)-interpretive lens from Cabitza and Locoro (2014) to a case of knowledge workers struggling with appropriation of UC&C for creating and sharing practice knowledge. We evaluate the framework - and discuss the usefulness of the lens in this specific setting. To further improve and enrich, we pose questions, aiming at contributing to the communication of valuable insights informing the design and use of future ITKAs in knowledge work.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Pries-Heje, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383681"],"event":{"end":"2015-11-14","place":"Lissabon, pt","start":"2015-11-12","title":"7th International Joint Conference on Knowledge Discovery, Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["IT knowledge Artefacts","Individual Practices","Knowledge creation","Situativity","Socio Technical Fit","UC C"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the misfits in knowledge work grasping the essence with the lens of the it knowledge artefact","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84960954273","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383681","identifier":[{"id":"84960954273","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a58dd1be-c2bb-4533-b9c2-18c894ffc8e5"],"keyword":["IT-knowledge Artefacts","Individual Practices","Knowledge Creation","Situativity","Socio-Technical Fit","UC&C"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F617D4FD38E2FD43E6B3D54189E6E3B5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ana","key":"fredpedh","last":"Fred","name":"Fred, Ana","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"dietzpedh","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"aveiropedh","last":"Aveiro","name":"Aveiro, David","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kecheng","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Kecheng","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joaquim","key":"felipepedh","last":"Felipe","name":"Felipe, Joaquim","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5220/0005662204360443","isbn":["9789897581588"],"pages":"436-443","place":"Lisbon - Portugal","publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 7th International Joint Conference on Knowledge Discovery, Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management","title":"IC3K 2015","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960954273"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a58dd1be-c2bb-4533-b9c2-18c894ffc8e5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Misfits in Knowledge Work : Grasping the Essence with the Lens of the IT Knowledge Artefact","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383681","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"How to increase knowledge workers productivity is still a puzzle. While knowledge work has become increasingly virtual, collaborative and interactive, we still witness challenges in the area of productivity. We challenge the widespread perception of the causal relationship between high autonomy and high productivity in knowledge work and the fact that configuration and standardization for improving productivity is logical impossible. With a hermeneutical approach we describe and interpret “what is going on” in two different context of interaction knowledge work. Findings suggests that knowledge workers often feel caught in counter-productive practices with technology, due to the autonomous use of Interaction-IT and the challenge of configuring work. We witness different behaviors related to “the autonomy paradox” and we see something interesting happening, when introducing Interaction IT. While configuring work should lower autonomy and negatively influence productivity, we see the opposite. While increased autonomy should increase the productivity, we also see the opposite. We interpret the findings as a balance between autonomy-loss and productivity gain - and as such deliver new insight on the autonomy paradox.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Pries-Heje, Lene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382881"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","end":"2015-08-12","place":"Oulu, fi","start":"2015-08-09","title":"The 38th Information Systems Research Conference in Scandinavia","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autonomy","Interaction IT","Productivity","Work practices","autonomy paradox","co configuring","interaction workers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co configuration in interaction work","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382881","ids":["itu-6c3e608f-586f-4bd1-a1c9-890bbcf1603a"],"keyword":["Interaction IT","autonomy","autonomy paradox","co-configuring","interaction workers","productivity","work-practices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E299A9785EDAE633592F7AC61289FA30"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Information Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a22e85da-82e3-410d-8ef1-31407362ba19","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","orcid":"0000-0001-7193-3797","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"prieshejepau","last":"Pries-Heje","name":"Pries-Heje, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"annsi","key":"ôörnipedh","last":"Ôörni","name":"Ôörni, annsi","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Netta","key":"livaripedh","last":"Livari","name":"Livari, Netta","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kari","key":"kuuttipedh","last":"Kuutti","name":"Kuutti, Kari","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Harri","key":"oinaskukkonenpedh","last":"Oinas-Kukkonen","name":"Oinas-Kukkonen, Harri","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Miko","key":"rajanenpedh","last":"Rajanen","name":"Rajanen, Miko","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789526209173"],"issn":["00000036"],"place":"Oulu, Finland, 9 - 12 August","series":"Proceedings / Information Systems Research In Scandinavia","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 38th Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia (IRIS 38)","volume":"IRIS 38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6c3e608f-586f-4bd1-a1c9-890bbcf1603a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Co-Configuration in Interaction Work","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382881","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This case addresses the ability of organisations to respond and drive change in a responsible manner, showing that the capacity to do so depends on the leader’s ability to see the bigger picture and to listen to wakeup calls in the industry. The issue is whether the leader has an autopilot mind-set vs one that continuously seeks awareness of the drivers of change and of the underlying reasons for this change. The case presents the difference in actions and results of key players on the American Automobile market during the period from around 1970 until 2012. We have chosen to take a look on the big three automakers of Detroit - General Motors, Chrysler and Ford - and the biggest Japanese Producers - Toyota and Honda. With the mindset in focus we are interested in what distinguish the actors at the US Car market, being either an 'American' or a 'Japanese' car manufacturer, and how it influences their ability to react responsibly.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fischer, Louise Harder","Heiberg, Birgitte"],"cuid":["S02-090.32-031089"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sustainability in the auto industry the significance of a leader s mindset","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-090.32-031089","ids":["cbs-05cf17c7-2903-4150-bcfc-7cc8038010d0","cbs-7e4336e6-0a29-40df-bbbf-63c5a099a068"],"lang":"English","level":"Educational","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-38D098E91339CD040607A3E7B61EE372"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of IT Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Harder","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Louise Harder","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Clement","key":"thaaruppau","last":"Thaarup","name":"Thaarup, Mikkel Clement","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"heibergpau","last":"Heiberg","name":"Heiberg, Birgitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Copenhagen Business School, CBS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-05cf17c7-2903-4150-bcfc-7cc8038010d0","cbs-7e4336e6-0a29-40df-bbbf-63c5a099a068"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Sustainability in the Auto Industry : The Significance of a Leader's Mindset","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.32-031089","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
